ergent for the development effort. The process may be sequential, in which each major phase (i.e., design, implement, and test) is completed before the next begins, but an iterative approach—where small aspects are separately designed, implemented, and tested—can reduce risk and cost and increase quality. ^ Dooley 2017 , p. 1.",
